🧠 Cognitive Pattern Explorer
Day 36/60 — #60DaysOfClaudeAI
A calm, game-like self-reflection experience that helps you notice how you tend to think — without labeling, scoring, or diagnosing you. Built as a single offline HTML file with zero frameworks.
✨ What it does
Instead of a quiz that hands you a verdict, Cognitive Pattern Explorer walks you through three short chapters and lets your choices reveal patterns:
Discover Your Thinking Style — six everyday scenarios, each with five response options mapped to a different thinking tendency.
Choose Your Priorities — drag-and-drop cards to rank what matters most to you when deciding something.
Map Your Thinking — arrange thought-fragments on a timeline in the order they naturally show up in your head.
At the end, a Reflection Journal shows a percentage breakdown across five tendencies, written in reflective language ("you often...", "this suggests...") rather than clinical labels.
The five thinking tendencies
🔵 Analytical Thinker
🌸 Emotional Intuitive
💜 Overthinking Loop Style
🟡 Action-First Decision Maker
🟢 Balanced Reflective Thinker
🎮 Features
Calm / Stress mode at the start — changes the pace and ambient animation intensity
Reusable drag-and-drop component — powers both the priority cards and the timeline, with:
Native HTML5 drag-and-drop (desktop)
Touch-based reordering (mobile)
Up/down buttons for full keyboard accessibility
Ambient orb — a soft background gradient that shifts color live toward whichever thinking style is currently leading, as a quiet visual signature
Progress tracker across all four stages (Discover → Priorities → Timeline → Reflection)
prefers-reduced-motion support — all animations and transitions are disabled automatically for users who need that
Fully responsive, down to small mobile screens
100% offline — no external fonts, CDNs, or dependencies
🛠️ Tech Stack
Vanilla HTML5
Vanilla CSS3 (custom properties, backdrop-filter, keyframe animations)
Vanilla JavaScript (ES5-friendly, no build step, no frameworks)
Single file: cognitive-pattern-explorer.html — just open it in any browser.
🚀 Usage
Bash
⚠️ A note on purpose
This app is built purely for self-exploration and curiosity. It is not a psychological assessment, diagnostic tool, or substitute for professional guidance. Think of it as a mirror, not a mark sheet.
